## CURRENT TASK — the one to pick up

User's request (verbatim-ish): *"a dropshadow behind all these paper ones… the way it was
handled on wolfspoint was a literal square with a super blurred bg that just followed the
shape and sat behind it, lowered opacity and blurred. then u don't have to worry about it
not working with the jagged edges. And for hover — same thing, no box-shadow, only our fake
shadow."*

**STATUS: the fix is ALREADY COMMITTED and pushed** — commit `540a424` ("Cast shadows as
blurred black layers behind torn clippings") implements exactly this via a dedicated
`.card-shadow` div:

```css
.card-shadow {
  position: absolute; inset: 0;
  background: rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
  clip-path: var(--tear);          /* traces the torn shape loosely */
  filter: blur(11px);
  transform: translateY(9px);
  opacity: 0.6; pointer-events: none;
  transition: transform var(--transition), filter var(--transition);
  z-index: 0;
}
/* hover pushes it down + softer: */
.project-card:hover .card-shadow { transform: translateY(16px); filter: blur(17px); }
```

The JS appends `<div class="card-shadow">` as the FIRST child inside each `.project-card`
and each About `.clip` (three insertion sites: card builder ~line 1300, about section clips
~line 1429, about sidebar clips ~line 1510 — line numbers in the COMMITTED version).

**⚠️ GOTCHA — the working tree is dirty.** `git status` shows `M index.html`: the file on
disk has been REVERTED back to the older `box-shadow: 0 10px 26px rgba(30,25,15,0.42);`
approach (probably a stale editor buffer saved over it — that's what the user saw in
devtools and why they said "that doesn't work"). `git diff index.html` shows the revert.
Almost certainly the right move is `git restore index.html` (discard the working-tree
revert so the committed `.card-shadow` version is what's on disk), then verify visually and
tell the user it's already live. Do NOT re-add box-shadow — user explicitly rejected it.
box-shadow on a clipped element paints a sharp rectangle and does NOT follow `clip-path`,
which is exactly the problem being avoided. Also note `.clip > *:not(.card-shadow)` must
stay (keeps the shadow under the content).

If the user wants tuning after seeing the real version: knobs are `blur(11px)`,
`opacity: 0.6`, `translateY(9px)`, and the hover values `translateY(16px)/blur(17px)`.

## Key architecture in index.html (line numbers ≈ committed 540a424 version)

- **CSS vars** (top of `<style>`): `--desk #1e1e1e`, `--paper #a59f96`, `--paper-light #c9c1b2`,
  `--ink #1a1a1a`, `--muted #59534a`, `--gold #9a7a33`, `--gold-light #d9b458`, `--cream #f0e7d3`,
  metal ring palettes `--gold-ol/-od/-mid/-il/-id` and `--sil-*` equivalents, `--font-head` (typewriter), `--transition`.
- **Sheet**: `.sheet` is the torn manila page (`clip-path: var(--tear)`, set in JS).
  `.sheet-wrap` has `pointer-events:none` so clicks fall through to tabs; `.sheet` re-enables
  them (clip-path makes hit-testing follow the paper). `.sheet-shadow` is a plain inset rect
  div behind the sheet with `box-shadow` — the SAME trick the user wants for cards.
- **Tabs**: `.tab-row` (margin-bottom −14px, z-index below sheet) → `.ftab` (silver rim) →
  `.ftab-in` (face; inactive `#3b362f` dark, active `var(--paper)` merging into sheet).
- **Cards**: `.project-card` children = `.card-shadow` (new), `.card-content` (photo+text,
  fades to opacity .18 on hover), `.card-actions` (revealed on hover). `--tear` set per card
  from `CLIP_VARIANTS` (6 seeded polygons). `.card-photo` sepia photo w/ white border.
- **Highlight cards**: `.project-card.highlight` — gilded frame, `filter: drop-shadow(...)`
  (correct choice — it's corner-MASKED so box-shadow would be clipped away anyway; the
  drop-shadow follows the scooped silhouette). Interior: `.highlight-surface` +
  `.highlight-media` (img) + `.highlight-body` + `.highlight-actions`. Spans 2 cols via
  `.projects-wrap[data-cols] .project-card.highlight { grid-column: span 2 }` (gated on
  data-cols — needed because span-2 creates implicit tracks that corrupt column detection).
- **Gilded buttons** `.gb`: `.gb-frame` (outer ring, scoop vars `--sr/--so/--sor` MUST be
  explicitly reset here — else it inherits scoop vars from `.highlight-surface` and corner
  radii break; this was a real bug, commit `806502e`), `::before`/`::after` middle/inner
  rings, `.gb-inner` face. Scoop = 4 radial-gradient corner masks per layer, `--r: 10px`.
  Variants: `.gb-silver` (GitHub links), `.gb-gold` (everything else).
- **Scoop-mask group rule** (~line 396): `.gb-frame, .gb-frame::before/after, .gb-inner,
  .project-card.highlight(::before/::after), .highlight-surface, ...` share a mask-image.
- **Archive modal**: same gilded frame treatment (dark header `#2e2a23`).
- **Collapse**: `.projects-wrap.collapsed` uses a `mask-image` linear-gradient "scroll
  shadow" (WolffsPoint ShadowScrollView technique — content dissolves, NOT a covering
  overlay; `--peek` px set from JS `PEEK_PX` const ~92). `.section-toggle` +
  `.show-more-btn` — DELIBERATELY DE-CHROMED (plain typewriter underline, no gilding).
  `.beyond-fold` cards get staggered `card-in` animation on expand.
- **About `.clip`**: torn clippings for About sections/sidebar; `.clip > *:not(.card-shadow)`
  keeps content above layers. Contact rows are plain hairline rows w/ gold icons (also
  de-chromed on purpose).
- **JS**: card building loop in `initializeSite` (~line 1230-1350). Button classifier:
  silver iff `new URL(href).hostname` ends with `github.com` OR has `fa-github` icon — do
  NOT substring-match "github" (github.io Pages URLs were falsely silvered — fixed `e20174d`).
  View swap ~line 1527: `startViewTransition` + JS height morph on `.sheet`; hash routing
  `#about`/`#projects`. `buildTornClipPath(w,h,seed,topDepthScale)` ~line 1566;
  `CLIP_VARIANTS` seeds [11,37,53,71,89,103]. Sheet tear is FROZEN across height changes —
  regenerates only on width change, quantized to 24px buckets, 150ms debounce (fixes edge
  jitter during height morph, commit `acdc464`). Column counting derives from grid width
  math, writes `data-cols` on `.projects-wrap`.

